 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 456645,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The average arrival rate of trucks at a truck loading station is 15 per day. Calculate the probability that 17 trucks arrive at the loading station on a particular day.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.085 "
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Apply the Poisson probability formula where <span data-math=\"\\mu  = 15\"></span> and <span data-math=\"x = 17\"></span>.<br>Substituting these values into the Poisson probability formula, the probability for 17 successes can be calculated as follows:<br><span data-math=\"P\\left( x \\right) = \\;\\frac{{{\\mu ^x}\\;{e^{ - \\mu }}}}{{x!}}\"></span><br>\n<span data-math=\"P\\left( {17} \\right) = \\;\\frac{{{{15}^{17}}\\;{e^{ - 15}}}}{{17!}} = 0.085\"></span><br>The same probability answer can be obtained using technology, as follows:<br><br>Excel: In any empty cell, type in the command:<br> \n=POISSON.DIST(17,15,FALSE)<br><br>\nPython:<br> \nType in the commands:<br>\n<pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\">from scipy.stats import poisson\npoisson.pmf(17, 15)\n\nThe resulting output will look like this:\n0.085\n</pre>\n\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
